const WORDS = [
['achieve','lograr','Goals','I want to achieve my goals.','Quiero lograr mis metas.'],['improve','mejorar','Goals','I wish I could improve my English faster.','Ojalá pudiera mejorar mi inglés más rápido.'],['effort','esfuerzo','Goals','Learning a language takes effort.','Aprender un idioma requiere esfuerzo.'],['confidence','confianza','Goals','Practice helps you build confidence.','La práctica te ayuda a ganar confianza.'],['challenge','reto','Goals','Speaking English is a challenge for me.','Hablar inglés es un reto para mí.'],['give up','rendirse','Goals',"If I were you, I wouldn’t give up.",'Si fuera tú, no me rendiría.'],['make progress','progresar','Goals','You have made a lot of progress.','Has progresado mucho.'],['skill','habilidad','Goals','Which skill would you like to improve?','¿Qué habilidad te gustaría mejorar?'],['mistake','error','Study','I wish I hadn’t made that mistake.','Ojalá no hubiera cometido ese error.'],['revise','repasar','Study','I need to revise for my exam.','Necesito repasar para mi examen.'],['take an exam','rendir un examen','Study','I am taking an exam tomorrow.','Mañana rindo un examen.'],['pass an exam','aprobar un examen','Study','If I studied more, I would pass the exam.','Si estudiara más, aprobaría el examen.'],['fail','desaprobar / fallar','Study','He might have failed the test.','Puede que haya desaprobado el examen.'],['hand in','entregar','Study','When do we have to hand in the essay?','¿Cuándo tenemos que entregar el ensayo?'],['figure out','resolver / entender','Study','I can’t figure out the answer.','No logro entender la respuesta.'],['look up','buscar información','Study','Look up the word in a dictionary.','Busca la palabra en un diccionario.'],['knowledge','conocimiento','Study','Reading helps you gain knowledge.','Leer te ayuda a adquirir conocimiento.'],['deadline','fecha límite','Study','I wish the deadline were later.','Ojalá la fecha límite fuera más tarde.'],['borrow','pedir prestado','Daily life','Could I borrow your pen?','¿Podría pedirte prestado tu bolígrafo?'],['lend','prestar','Daily life','Could you lend me your notes?','¿Podrías prestarme tus apuntes?'],['afford','poder permitirse económicamente','Daily life',"I wish I could afford a new laptop.",'Ojalá pudiera permitirme una laptop nueva.'],['save up','ahorrar para algo','Daily life','I am saving up for a trip.','Estoy ahorrando para un viaje.'],['run out of','quedarse sin','Daily life','We have run out of milk.','Nos hemos quedado sin leche.'],['turn down','rechazar','Daily life','Why did she turn down the offer?','¿Por qué rechazó la oferta?'],['look after','cuidar','Daily life','Who looks after your dog?','¿Quién cuida a tu perro?'],['get along with','llevarse bien con','Daily life','I get along with my classmates.','Me llevo bien con mis compañeros.'],['used to','solía','Daily life','I used to walk to school.','Solía caminar a la escuela.'],['instead of','en vez de','Daily life','Try speaking instead of translating.','Intenta hablar en vez de traducir.'],['although','aunque','Connectors','Although it was difficult, I tried.','Aunque era difícil, lo intenté.'],['however','sin embargo','Connectors','It was late. However, we continued.','Era tarde. Sin embargo, continuamos.'],['unless','a menos que','Connectors','I won’t go unless you come with me.','No iré a menos que vengas conmigo.'],['therefore','por lo tanto','Connectors','It was raining; therefore, we stayed home.','Llovía; por lo tanto, nos quedamos en casa.'],['because of','debido a','Connectors','We were late because of the traffic.','Llegamos tarde debido al tráfico.'],['as soon as','tan pronto como','Connectors','Call me as soon as you arrive.','Llámame tan pronto como llegues.'],['even though','a pesar de que','Connectors','Even though I was tired, I studied.','A pesar de que estaba cansado, estudié.'],['otherwise','de lo contrario','Connectors','Hurry up; otherwise, we’ll be late.','Apúrate; de lo contrario, llegaremos tarde.'],['exhausted','agotado','Feelings','She must have been exhausted after work.','Debe de haber estado agotada después del trabajo.'],['disappointed','decepcionado','Feelings','I was disappointed with my result.','Estaba decepcionado con mi resultado.'],['relieved','aliviado','Feelings','I felt relieved after the exam.','Me sentí aliviado después del examen.'],['worried','preocupado','Feelings','What are you worried about?','¿Qué te preocupa?'],['proud','orgulloso','Feelings','I am proud of my progress.','Estoy orgulloso de mi progreso.'],['embarrassed','avergonzado','Feelings','I felt embarrassed when I forgot his name.','Me sentí avergonzado cuando olvidé su nombre.'],['upset','molesto / afectado','Feelings','She might have been upset about the news.','Puede que las noticias la hayan afectado.'],['grateful','agradecido','Feelings','I am grateful for your help.','Estoy agradecido por tu ayuda.'],['evidence','prueba / evidencia','Deduction','There is no evidence that he was there.','No hay pruebas de que estuviera allí.'],['clue','pista','Deduction','This message is an important clue.','Este mensaje es una pista importante.'],['likely','probable','Deduction','It is likely that she missed the bus.','Es probable que haya perdido el bus.'],['certain','seguro / cierto','Deduction','I am certain he was at home.','Estoy seguro de que estaba en casa.'],['missing','desaparecido / que falta','Deduction','My keys are missing.','No encuentro mis llaves.'],['belong to','pertenecer a','Deduction','Who does this bag belong to?','¿A quién pertenece este bolso?'],['realize','darse cuenta','Deduction','I realized I had left my phone at home.','Me di cuenta de que había dejado mi teléfono en casa.'],['doubt','duda','Deduction','There is no doubt about it.','No hay duda al respecto.'],['miss','perder / no alcanzar','Travel','He must have missed the train.','Debe de haber perdido el tren.'],['get lost','perderse','Travel','We might have got lost.','Puede que nos hayamos perdido.'],['set off','salir / emprender el viaje','Travel','What time did you set off?','¿A qué hora saliste?'],['delay','retraso','Travel','There was a delay at the airport.','Hubo un retraso en el aeropuerto.'],['abroad','en el extranjero','Travel','If I had more money, I would study abroad.','Si tuviera más dinero, estudiaría en el extranjero.'],['accommodation','alojamiento','Travel','We need to find accommodation.','Necesitamos encontrar alojamiento.'],['journey','trayecto / viaje','Travel','How long was the journey?','¿Cuánto duró el trayecto?'],['arrive','llegar','Travel','She can’t have arrived yet; her flight is still in the air.','No puede haber llegado todavía; su vuelo sigue en el aire.']
].map((w,i)=>({id:'w'+i,en:w[0],es:w[1],cat:w[2],example:w[3],translation:w[4]}));
const TOPICS={wish:{title:'Patterns after wish',desc:'Deseos, arrepentimientos y cosas que cambiarías.',icon:'✧',rules:[['Un presente diferente','wish + past simple','I wish I had more time.','Ojalá tuviera más tiempo. El pasado expresa una situación irreal ahora. Con be, were es la opción formal: I wish I were taller.'],['Arrepentimiento del pasado','wish + past perfect','I wish I had studied harder.','Ojalá hubiera estudiado más. Se usa had + participio para algo pasado que ya no puedes cambiar.'],['Una conducta que quieres cambiar','wish + would + verb','I wish my neighbours would stop shouting.','Ojalá mis vecinos dejaran de gritar. Se usa para quejas o cambios deseados, normalmente sobre otra persona.'],['Una capacidad que deseas','wish + could + verb','I wish I could speak fluently.','Ojalá pudiera hablar con fluidez. Could expresa capacidad o posibilidad deseada.']]},second:{title:'Second conditional',desc:'Imagina situaciones y sus resultados.',icon:'↗',rules:[['Una situación hipotética','If + past simple, would + verb','If I had more time, I would practise every day.','Si tuviera más tiempo, practicaría cada día. Hablas del presente o futuro imaginario o poco probable.'],['Dar un consejo','If I were you, I would…','If I were you, I would revise these words.','Si fuera tú, repasaría estas palabras. En exámenes, usa were para hipótesis con be.'],['Pregunta y variaciones','What would you do if…?','What would you do if you won a prize?','Would va en el resultado, no normalmente después de if. Could expresa capacidad y might una posibilidad en el resultado.']]},modals:{title:'Past modals of deduction',desc:'¿Qué pudo haber pasado? Sigue las pistas.',icon:'⌕',rules:[['Una conclusión muy segura','must have + past participle','The ground is wet. It must have rained.','Debe de haber llovido. Es una deducción fuerte sobre el pasado, no una obligación.'],['Una posibilidad','might / may / could have + past participle','She might have missed the bus.','Puede que haya perdido el bus. No estás seguro. Estas formas pueden expresar posibilidad pasada.'],['Una conclusión negativa muy segura',"can’t / couldn’t have + past participle",'He can’t have taken it; he was abroad.','No puede haberlo tomado; estaba en el extranjero. Consideras imposible esa explicación.'],['Cuidado con el tiempo','present: must be → past: must have been','She must be tired. → She must have been tired.','Para el pasado necesitas have + participio: gone, seen, taken, forgotten, been. Mustn’t expresa prohibición, no deducción negativa.']]},wh:{title:'WH questions',desc:'Construye preguntas y mantén la conversación.',icon:'?',rules:[['Preguntar por información','WH + auxiliary + subject + verb?','Where did you go yesterday?','What: qué · Where: dónde · When: cuándo · Why: por qué · Who: quién · Which: cuál · Whose: de quién · How: cómo. Después de did, el verbo va en forma base.'],['Preguntar por el sujeto','Who / What + verb?','Who called you?','Si who es el sujeto, no añadas do/did: Who called you? Si preguntas por el objeto: Who did you call?'],['Preguntas con be y modales','WH + be/modal + subject…?','Why were you late? / What would you change?','Con be no uses do/did. Con modales, coloca el modal antes del sujeto.'],['Cantidad, frecuencia y duración','How much / many / often / long…?','How often do you practise?','How much: cantidad no contable o precio. How many: contables. How often: frecuencia. How long: duración.']]}};
const QUESTIONS=[];
function add(topic,prompt,options,answer,explanation){QUESTIONS.push({id:'q'+QUESTIONS.length,topic,prompt,options,answer,explanation});}
add('wish','I don’t have much free time. I wish I ___ more time.',['have','had','would have'],'had','Deseo sobre el presente: wish + past simple.');
add('wish','I failed yesterday. I wish I ___ harder.',['studied','had studied','would study'],'had studied','Arrepentimiento sobre el pasado: wish + had + participio.');
add('wish','My neighbours keep shouting. I wish they ___ shouting.',['would stop','had stopped','will stop'],'would stop','Pides un cambio de conducta: wish + would + verbo base.');
add('wish','I can’t swim. I wish I ___ swim.',['can','could','will'],'could','Una capacidad que deseas ahora: wish + could.');
add('wish','I’m not tall. I wish I ___ taller. (Forma formal)',['am','were','had been'],'were','Para un presente irreal, were es la forma formal con be.');
add('wish','I told her a secret yesterday. I wish I ___ her.',['didn’t tell','hadn’t told','wouldn’t tell'],'hadn’t told','Te arrepientes de algo que ya hiciste: wish + past perfect negativo.');
add('wish','He never listens to me. I wish he ___ to me.',['would listen','listens','had listened'],'would listen','Es una queja sobre su conducta habitual y un deseo de cambio.');
add('wish','I live far from school. I wish I ___ closer.',['live','lived','had lived'],'lived','Quieres que tu situación actual fuera diferente: past simple.');
add('wish','I missed the train this morning. I wish I ___ earlier.',['had left','leave','would leave'],'had left','Desear cambiar un hecho pasado requiere had + participio.');
add('wish','I don’t understand this word. I wish I ___ what it meant.',['know','knew','had known'],'knew','No entiendes ahora: wish + pasado simple, knew.');
add('second','If I ___ more money, I would travel abroad.',['have','had','would have'],'had','If + past simple; would + verbo base en el resultado.');
add('second','If she studied more, she ___ better results.',['gets','will get','would get'],'would get','El resultado hipotético se expresa con would + verbo base.');
add('second','If I ___ you, I would talk to the teacher.',['were','am','will be'],'were','If I were you es la fórmula habitual para dar un consejo.');
add('second','What would you do if you ___ your phone?',['lose','lost','would lose'],'lost','Después de if usa el pasado simple: lost.');
add('second','If it didn’t rain, we ___ for a walk.',['would go','went','will go'],'would go','La situación imaginaria tiene un resultado: would go.');
add('second','If he ___ closer, we would see him more often.',['lives','would live','lived'],'lived','La condición irreal usa past simple: lived.');
add('second','I ___ that if I were you.',['wouldn’t do','didn’t do','won’t do'],'wouldn’t do','Consejo negativo: would not + verbo base.');
add('second','If you could live anywhere, where ___?',['you would live','would you live','did you lived'],'would you live','En preguntas, would va antes del sujeto: where would you live?');
add('second','If I knew her number, I ___ her.',['would call','called','call'],'would call','Resultado hipotético: would call.');
add('second','Which sentence is correct?',['If I would study, I passed.','If I studied, I would pass.','If I study, I would passed.'],'If I studied, I would pass.','Second conditional: if + past simple, would + infinitivo sin to.');
add('modals','His shoes are wet and muddy. He ___ through the rain. (Conclusión muy segura)',['must have walked','might walk','must walk'],'must have walked','Deducción fuerte sobre algo pasado: must have + participio.');
add('modals','I’m not sure why Ana is late. She ___ the bus. (Posibilidad pasada)',['must miss','might have missed','can’t have missed'],'might have missed','Might have expresa una explicación posible, sin certeza.');
add('modals','He was in Peru all day yesterday. He ___ at the London meeting in person.',['must have been','might have been','can’t have been'],'can’t have been','Las pruebas descartan esa posibilidad pasada: can’t have been.');
add('modals','The lights were off, and nobody answered. They ___ out. (Conclusión muy segura)',['must have gone','must go','must have went'],'must have gone','Después de have necesitas el participio: gone, no went.');
add('modals','She looks upset. She ___ some bad news. (Solo es posible)',['might have received','can’t have received','must receive'],'might have received','No tienes certeza: might have + received.');
add('modals','I saw him eat a big lunch. He ___ hungry just afterwards. (Lo consideras imposible)',['must have been','can’t have been','might be'],'can’t have been','Deducción negativa sobre el pasado: can’t have been.');
add('modals','Which phrase describes a strong past deduction?',['must have forgotten','must forget','must have forgot'],'must have forgotten','El participio de forget es forgotten.');
add('modals','There is no milk left. Someone ___ it. (Conclusión muy segura)',['must have drunk','must have drank','must drink'],'must have drunk','Drink → drank → drunk. Usa el participio después de have.');
add('modals','Perhaps I left my keys at work. I ___ them there.',['might have left','can’t have left','must leave'],'might have left','Perhaps indica posibilidad: might have left.');
add('modals','Past deduction: “She must be tired” becomes…',['She must have been tired.','She must had been tired.','She must have be tired.'],'She must have been tired.','Modal + have + been: have no cambia después del modal.');
add('wh','___ did you go last weekend? — To the beach.',['Where','When','Who'],'Where','To the beach indica lugar: pregunta con where.');
add('wh','___ do you practise English? — Every day.',['How long','How often','How much'],'How often','Every day expresa frecuencia: how often.');
add('wh','Choose the correct question.',['Where did you went?','Where did you go?','Where you went?'],'Where did you go?','Did ya marca el pasado; el verbo principal queda en forma base.');
add('wh','___ called you last night? — My sister.',['Who','Who did','Whose'],'Who','Who es el sujeto: Who called you? No necesitas did.');
add('wh','___ bag is this? — It’s mine.',['Who','Whose','Which of'],'Whose','Whose pregunta por posesión: ¿de quién?');
add('wh','___ have you studied English? — For three years.',['How often','How many','How long'],'How long','For three years es duración: how long.');
add('wh','___ were you late? — Because I missed the bus.',['Why','What','Where'],'Why','Because introduce una razón: pregunta con why.');
add('wh','___ books did you buy? — Three.',['How much','How many','How long'],'How many','Books es contable plural: how many.');
add('wh','Choose the correct question.',['What you would do?','What would you do?','What would do you?'],'What would you do?','WH + modal + sujeto + verbo: What would you do?');
add('wh','___ does this cost? — Ten dollars.',['How much','How many','How often'],'How much','Para preguntar por el precio usa how much.');
const SPEAKING=[['What would you do if you had a month off?','I would… if I had…','I would travel around Peru if I had a month off. I would visit new places and practise English with other travellers.','second'],['What do you wish you could do better?','I wish I could… because…','I wish I could speak English more confidently because I want to meet people from other countries.','wish'],['You called a friend, but they didn’t answer. What might have happened?','They might have… / They must have…','They might have left their phone at home. They might have been busy studying. I don’t have enough evidence to be sure.','modals'],['Where would you live if you could live anywhere? Why?','If I could…, I would… because…','If I could live anywhere, I would live near the sea because I enjoy swimming and warm weather.','second'],['What do you wish you had done differently last week?','I wish I had…','I wish I had revised more vocabulary last week. I spent too much time on my phone.','wish'],['Ask a friend about their last holiday. Use three WH questions.','Where did…? / Who did…? / How long…?','Where did you go? Who did you travel with? How long did you stay there?','wh'],['Your friend got full marks after studying every day. Make a strong past deduction.','They must have…','They must have worked really hard. They must have understood the questions well.','modals'],['What would you change about your daily routine?','If I…, I would…','If I had more free time, I would exercise every morning. I would also read a little in English.','second']];
